! ax4b_5a_p_field_000.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148 (1248,
! "INDEX MODIFICATION TEST", banner PDF p.113), TEST 5 "CHECKS ALL 8
! CODES IN THE P FIELD OF A VFL LOAD", block TEST 5A "CHKS P FIELD OF
! 000":
!
!   PDF p.142  010736.40-010767.00  the whole block
!   PDF p.153  011351.00            148K24, the word it loads
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi, the driver at 400
! dpi; checked row for row against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax4b_5a_p_field_000_listing.py (46 rows, 5 symbols).
!
! WHAT IT TESTS (IBM's code, unchanged).  Z,$X1 zeroes index register 1;
!   L(BU),148K24($X1)   11351.00 81 000000.20 50   I = 1, P = 0
! must load 148K24 (indexing by zero) and leave $X1 alone -- P = 0 is
! not progressive.  "LX,$X0,$R" puts the result in index register 0,
! and KV/KC on $X0 compare its value and count with 148K24's.  The
! failure branches sort the cause: "LOADS OK BUT MODIFIES IX REG" (X1
! changed), "ACTS LIKE A P OF 100" (KVI: the address itself was
! loaded), "ACTS LIKE P OF 001, 010, 011, 101, 110, OR 111", "LOADED
! FROM I-LEFT INDEX VALUE ADR BUT DID NOT MODIFY IX REG", "LOADED FROM
! UNKNOWN LOCN ...".  It needs $X0 to be a real, writable register:
! LX,$X0 and the later "L(BU),$X0" (address 20 octal) both use it.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SEN "1310.00 80",
!     SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80"); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44,
!     read in the page image), so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the
!     error entry on a failure.
!   * IC248 and BIT21 are SYN'd from the printed "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32
!     10) and "V+,$X13,BIT21" (13101.32 B0); the continuity rows after
!     B,SSW are never run.
!   * Notation only: the page's "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")";
!     the label glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I48..),
!     as for every ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  Nothing
!     else changed.
!
! RESULT ON THE MODEL, 2026-11-18 (a57832f + this deck): PASSES -- halts
! at SSW (PC 1410), SEN = 0, $X0 = 148K24's word (0x29CBBE029CB80000,
! as LX,$X0,$R must leave it for KV and KC to match), $X1 = 0.  CYCLES
! 219 is MODEL BEHAVIOUR; no time is printed.  IBM's listing and the
! model AGREE.
!
! INJECTIONS, each in a scratch copy of bsv/, OBSERVED for this deck:
!   P = 0 treated as immediate (vi.a.p == 4 || == 0) -> FAIL halt, SEN
!     010750.40: "P OF 000 ACTS LIKE A P OF 100.", CYCLES 165.
!   writes to X0 discarded (writeIndex j == 0) -> FAIL halt, SEN 010757.00:
!     "LOADED FROM I-LEFT INDEX VALUE ADR BUT DID NOT MODIFY IX REG", CYCLES 256.
!   I = 0 indexed by X0 (effAddrSigned's idx == 0 case removed) -> FAIL halt,
!     CYCLES 201; SEN stays 0 -- INFERRED, not dumped: SIC,SEN is then itself
!     indexed by X0 and stores elsewhere.
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model, the pins below (PASS, SEN = 0).
!   Each built in a scratch copy of bsv/ and restored (cmp IDENTICAL).
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
! The addresses are the ones this listing prints for them (SIC,SEN
! "1310.00 80", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80", B,SSW
! "1301.10 00"), the same as routine 148's; what is AT them is SSIP's,
! which this file replaces with halts, as ax4b_148_immediate_indexed does.
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! IC248, the continuity word, and BIT21: SYN from the printed addresses
! of "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32 10) and "V+,$X13,BIT21" (13101.32 B0); the
! three continuity rows that name them are never reached here (SSW
! halts first).
IC248   SYN, (8)11306.0
BIT21   SYN, (8)13101.0
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.142, 010736.40-010767.00 (no printed page number on the sheet)
! ======================================================================
!                                     ! -TEST 5 CHECKS ALL 8 CODES
!                                     ! -IN THE P FIELD OF A VFL LOAD.
        SLC, (8)10736.40
I4833   Z,   $X1                      ! -TEST 5A CHKS P FIELD OF 000.
        L(BU), I48K24($X1)
        LX,  $X0, $R
        KV,  $X0, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.0
        B,   I4834
        KC,  $X0, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.0
        B,   I4834
        L(BU), $X1
        BRZ, I4835                    ! -P OF 000 ALL OK.
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -P OF 000 LOADS OK BUT MODIFIES IX
        B,   SERS                     ! -REG SPECIFIED BY I-LEFT.
        B,   I4835
!
I4834   KVI, $X0, I48K24
        BZXE, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN                      ! -P OF 000 ACTS LIKE
        B,   SERS                     ! -A P OF 100.
        B,   I4835
!
        L(BU), $X0
        BRZ, $+1.0
        B,   I4836
        L(BU), $X1
        BRZ, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN                      ! -P OF 000 ACTS LIKE P OF 001, 010,
        B,   SERS                     ! -011,101,110, OR 111.
        B,   I4835
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOADED FROM I-LEFT INDEX VALUE ADR
        B,   SERS                     ! -BUT DID NOT MODIFY IX REG,
        B,   I4835
!
I4836   L(BU), $X1
        BRZ, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOADED FROM UNKNOWN LOCN BUT DID
        B,   SERS                     ! -MODIFY IX REG SPECIFIED BY I-LEFT.
        B,   I4835
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOADED FROM UNKNOWN LOCN,DID NOT
        B,   SERS                     ! -MODIFY IX REG SPECIFIED BY I-LEFT.
!
I4835   B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I4833
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B,   SSW                      ! -TO SSIP
        BD,  $+.32
!
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        V+,  $X13, BIT21
        SX,  $X13, IC248
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.153, 011351.00: the one constant TEST 5A reads
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)11351.0
I48K24  XW,  (8)123456.76, (8)123456, 0
        END, I4833
